  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Subsurface Mooring Data from the Bering Sea: Station Inner Front 4",
  "description": "Subsurface mooring data from the Bering Sea: Station Inner Front 4. Data were collected from 1994 through 2004. Sampled months varied through the years but were usually during April and June. Fluorometer, salinity, temperature, and UV vector data were collected at various depths throughout the years using instruments such as MTR, RCM-7, RCM-9, and SEACAT. 46m was the maximum bottom depth.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To collect physical oceanographic properties at and near the mooring locations.",
